From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 16:13:30 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 35/36] PS2: read the pad buffer through the uncached address

The IOP writes pad data into the buffer by DMA. Passing the cached address
let the EE keep returning the first (idle) value from its data cache, so
buttons never changed. Pass UNCACHED_SEG(buffer) to padPortOpen instead.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_019yH2brr5GjCGyCE62bYyXR
---
 src/Ps2Pad.cpp | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/Ps2Pad.cpp b/src/Ps2Pad.cpp
index f961de0..754ad14 100644
--- a/src/Ps2Pad.cpp
+++ b/src/Ps2Pad.cpp
@@ -5,6 +5,7 @@
 #include <cstdio>
 #include <libpad.h>
 #include <loadfile.h>
+#include <kernel.h>
 #include <sifrpc.h>
 
 void Ps2SifInitOnce(); // ps2boot.cpp
@@ -41,7 +42,9 @@ bool Ps2Pad::Init()
         return false;
     }
     padInit(0);
-    int r = padPortOpen(0, 0, s_PadBuf);
+    // The IOP writes pad data straight into this buffer by DMA. Read it through the uncached alias, otherwise the EE
+    // can keep returning the first (idle) value from its data cache.
+    int r = padPortOpen(0, 0, UNCACHED_SEG(s_PadBuf));
     printf("Ps2Pad: padPortOpen -> %d\n", r);
     if (r == 0)
         return false;
